   "text": "I read the structure in five parts and wrote them out in order.\n\n- **VHL ligand (left):** a 4-hydroxyproline carboxamide, with the OH hashed. The proline nitrogen is acylated by a 2-(isoxazol-5-yl)-3-methylbutanoyl group. The amide NH is attached to a (1-arylethyl) group whose aryl is a phenyl bearing 4-methylthiazol-5-yl.\n- **Linker:** the isoxazole carries a 3-O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013 chain to a piperidine nitrogen. The piperidine 4-oxygen is bonded to a cyclobutane that is 1,3-disubstituted with one hashed and one wedged O, so it is trans. The other cyclobutane oxygen is bonded to the 2-position of a pyridine.\n- **Bicycle:** pyridine C4 is bonded to the bridging N8 of a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane. Its N3 is bonded to the pyridazine.\n- **Pyridazine:** it carries an NH2 next to the ring nitrogen. At the other end it bears a phenyl ring with an ortho O\u2013P(=O)(OH)2 group.\n- **Stereochemistry:** I worked out the isoxazolyl CH and the cyclobutane descriptors from the wedges and hashes in the drawing. The hydroxyproline and the arylethyl centre follow the standard VHL ligand pattern, which I took as matching the drawing rather than rederiving. The bicycle is drawn without stereo, so none is assigned.\n\nI checked ring closures and numbering by hand, but did not run the SMILES through a parser.\n\nSMILES: Cc1ncsc1-c1ccc(cc1)[C@H](C)NC(=O)[C@@H]1C[C@@H](O)CN1C(=O)[C@H](C(C)C)c1cc(OCCN2CCC(CC2)O[C@H]2C[C@@H](C2)Oc2cc(ccn2)N2C3CCC2CN(C3)c2cc(nnc2N)-c2ccccc2OP(=O)(O)O)no1"
